---
import Button from '../../../components/Button.astro';
import DocumentLayout from '../../../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import ContentCard from '../../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import inventory from '../../../../public/graphs/working/coverage-inventory.json';
const names = {'same-id-rewritten': 'Earlier revision', 'restored-with-evidence-repair': 'Restored question'};
const rows = inventory.originalQuestions;
---
<DocumentLayout title="Graph coverage ledger" description="Analysis, repaired definitions and independent review status for all 588 original TENSOR questions in the 609-question working draft." canonicalPath="/graphs/coverage/">
  <ContentCard>
    <p class="section-kicker">Working graph · Question review</p>
    <h2>Coverage and revision status</h2>
    <p>The working graph contains <strong>609 questions and 1,953 routes</strong>: all 588 original IDs and 21 additional questions. This ledger links each original prompt to its current definition, evidence focus, review rationale, and scenario references.</p>
    <p>Every original has an author-reviewed entry. External domain approval and equivalent investigative coverage remain open. The sixteen <a href="/graphs/profiles/">event profiles</a> supply additional contexts for state changes, autonomous actions, unavailable content, and other events.</p>
    <div class="cta-group"><Button variant="primary" href="/graphs/?graph=working">Working graph</Button><Button variant="secondary" href="/graphs/?graph=published">Published graph</Button><Button variant="secondary" href="/graphs/working/coverage-inventory.json" download>Download ledger</Button></div>
    <h2>Original and revised questions</h2>
    <p><strong>{inventory.summary.authorReviewedDispositions} author-reviewed entries; {inventory.summary.approvedSemanticDispositions} externally approved.</strong> Source prompts, changed meaning, issues and target wording are available for every original. The downloaded ledger also includes the earlier revision stages.</p>
    <div class="coverage-filters"><label>Search originals<input id="coverage-search" type="search" placeholder="ID, domain, topic, or prompt" /></label><label>Lineage<select id="coverage-status" aria-label="Lineage"><option value="">All stages</option>{Object.entries(names).map(([value,label])=><option value={value}>{label}</option>)}</select></label></div>
    <p id="coverage-count" aria-live="polite">588 original questions</p>
    <div class="coverage-table coverage-ledger" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All original questions and their lineage">
      <table><thead><tr><th>Original question</th><th>Domain / stage</th><th>Revision group</th><th>Review and changes</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map((row) => <tr id={row.sourceId} data-coverage-row data-status={row.lineageStatus}><td><a href={`/graphs/?graph=published&node=${row.sourceId}`}>{row.sourceId} · {row.sourceLabel}</a><details><summary>Original prompt</summary><p>{row.sourceText}</p></details></td><td>{row.category}<br /><small>{row.archetype}</small></td><td>{names[row.lineageStatus]}{row.activeId && <p><a href={`/graphs/?graph=working&node=${row.activeId}`}>Working definition ↗</a></p>}</td><td><strong>{row.disposition === 'restore-with-evidence-repair' ? 'Revised and restored' : 'Prior evidence repair retained'}</strong><p>{row.sourceFacet}</p><details><summary>Meaning and identified issues</summary><p>{row.rationale}</p>{row.applicabilityLimitations?.map(limit => <p><strong>Applicability:</strong> {limit}</p>)}<ul>{row.issues.map(issue => <li>{issue}</li>)}</ul>{row.sourceDuplicateIds.length > 1 && <p>Repeated prompt IDs: {row.sourceDuplicateIds.join(', ')}. Equivalent meaning has not been established.</p>}<p>{row.scenarioRefs.length} scenario references in the complete analysis.</p></details><small>Agent review recorded · external domain review pending</small></td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
    </div>
    <p><strong>{inventory.summary.absentOriginal} original IDs absent.</strong> ID restoration and equivalent investigative coverage are separate measures.</p>
    <h2>Revision history</h2>
<div class="coverage-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Questions</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Published release</td><td>588</td><td>Preserved source baseline</td></tr><tr><td>Earlier technical reduction</td><td>219</td><td>369 original IDs removed</td></tr><tr><td>Entry evidence repairs</td><td>184</td><td>49 originals detached; 14 questions added</td></tr><tr><td>Positive evidence repairs</td><td>103</td><td>88 originals detached; 7 questions added</td></tr><tr><td>Original-question restoration</td><td>609</td><td>506 originals revised and returned; prior repairs retained</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <p>The source has 479 distinct exact prompts and 107 repeated-prompt groups involving 216 IDs. The ledger retains repeated wording and records changes in meaning rather than assuming equivalence from an ID match.</p>
    <h2>Evaluation records</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/graphs/working/reviews/2026-10-12-independent-review/README.md">seven-domain route review</a> records a separate agent challenge and repaired route defects. The <a href="/graphs/working/reviews/2026-10-12-restoration/README.md">restoration report</a> and <a href="/graphs/working/reviews/2026-10-12-restoration/analysis.json" download>per-ID analysis</a> document the question revisions. Regression evidence includes 1,791 authored graph scenarios and 144 event-profile scenarios.</p>
    <p>These evaluations use supplied observations and assessments. External review, authorized field cases, and independent record exchange are separate evaluation steps. <a href="/docs/graph-coverage-roadmap.md">The coverage roadmap</a> records the remaining review work.</p>
    <h2>Source pins</h2>
    <p>Published {inventory.published.version}: <code>{inventory.published.sha256}</code></p>
    <p>Working {inventory.working.version}: <code>{inventory.working.sha256}</code></p>
    <p><a href="/docs/legacy-migration.md">Preservation and migration method</a>. Reproduce the inventory with <code>python3 scripts/audit_graph_coverage.py --check</code> in a Framework checkout with full Git history. The inventory records source identity and revision history.</p>
  </ContentCard>
</DocumentLayout>
<script>
  const search = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#coverage-search');
  const status = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#coverage-status');
  const rows = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLTableRowElement>('[data-coverage-row]')];
  const apply = () => {
    let count = 0;
    for (const row of rows) {
      row.hidden = !row.textContent?.toLowerCase().includes(search?.value.trim().toLowerCase() || '') || Boolean(status?.value && row.dataset.status !== status.value);
      if (!row.hidden) count++;
    }
    const result = document.querySelector('#coverage-count');
    if (result) result.textContent = `${count} of 588 original questions`;
  };
  search?.addEventListener('input', apply); status?.addEventListener('change', apply);
</script>
<style>
  .coverage-table { overflow: auto; margin: 1rem 0; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .85rem; text-align: left; }
  tr[id] { scroll-margin-top: 6rem; }
  th, td { padding: .8rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: var(--bg-card); }
  .coverage-ledger { max-height: 42rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-soft); }
  .coverage-ledger th { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 1; }
  .coverage-ledger td:first-child { min-width: 15rem; max-width: 35rem; }
  details { margin-top: .4rem; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: .75rem; }
  .coverage-filters { display: flex; gap: 1rem; }
  .coverage-filters label { display: block; flex: 1; font-size: .8rem; }
  input, select { display: block; width: 100%; margin: .4rem 0; }
  .coverage-plan li { margin: 1rem 0; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .coverage-filters { flex-direction: column; } }
</style>
